# Iteration 1: Topk Retrieval vs Label Lists

## i01_0_retrieve_topk (59.0%, +6.9 Δ)
**Mechanism (Axis C):** Retrieved top-k most similar examples (Jaccard overlap) instead of using all. 
**Result:** Solid improvement; context dropped from 18K to 2.5K chars.
**Why it worked:** Limiting scope keeps model inside effective context window; similarity filtering removes distracting examples.
**Trade-off:** Lower cost, good accuracy—became backbone for iteration 2.

## i01_1_label_list (39.6%, -12.5 Δ)  
**Mechanism (Axis A):** Show only a list of all learned labels, no demonstrations.
**Result:** Severe regression; model exhibits label bias (predicts same label regardless of input).
**Why it failed:** Model cannot discriminate without concrete examples. Labels alone are too abstract.
**Takeaway:** Examples are necessary; but more examples (fewshot_all) is not better than selective (topk).

